hema validation against official GitHub Actions schema with exit code behavior matching the claim\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The research document and GitHub repository documentation confirm that wrkflw validate performs JSON Schema validation with the exact exit codes specified.\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: research/developer-tools/wrkflw.md lines 68-76 (accessed 2026-04-25)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: Read and cross-checked against github.com/bahdotsh/wrkflw on 2026-04-25\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM 4: wrkflw version 0.8.0 (latest as of item creation) is available via `cargo install wrkflw` or `brew install wrkflw`.\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: /home/user/claude_skills/research/developer-tools/wrkflw.md (lines 36-37)\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-04-25\\n  - Content: |\\n      **Latest version**: 0.8.0 (released 2026-04-22)\\n      **Installation**: `cargo install wrkflw` or `brew install wrkflw`\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: /home/user/claude_skills/research/developer-tools/wrkflw.md (lines 276-290, Installation section)\\n  - Finding: Installation section repeats the installation methods with additional build-from-source option, confirming cargo and Homebrew availability\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The research document explicitly lists version 0.8.0 as latest (released 2026-04-22) with installation methods via cargo and Homebrew.\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: research/developer-tools/wrkflw.md lines 36-37 (accessed 2026-04-25)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: Read on 2026-04-25\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM 5: actionlint has a native pre-commit hook available (at rhysd/actionlint on GitHub).\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/.pre-commit-hooks.yaml\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-04-25\\n  - Content: |\\n      actionlint repository contains a .pre-commit-hooks.yaml file that defines three pre-commit hooks:\\n      1. actionlint (Golang-based)\\n      2. actionlint-docker (Docker image-based, version 1.7.12)\\n      3. actionlint-system (system language hook for locally installed binary)\\n      All target YAML files matching pattern ^\\\\.github/workflows/\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint (main repository page)\\n  - Finding: Repository is confirmed to exist at rhysd/actionlint; documentation mentions \\\"integrations with reviewdog, Problem Matchers, super-linter, pre-commit, VS Code\\\"\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The actionlint GitHub repository at rhysd/actionlint contains a .pre-commit-hooks.yaml file with multiple pre-commit hook definitions, confirming native pre-commit support.\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/.pre-commit-hooks.yaml (accessed 2026-04-25)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: WebFetch on 2026-04-25\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM 6: prek (the pre-commit replacement used in this repo) is compatible with pre-commit hook format including `language: system` hooks.\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: https://prek.j178.dev/languages/ (Prek Language Support documentation)\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-04-25\\n  - Content: |\\n      \\\"system\\\" runs a system executable without a managed environment. The command is taken from 'entry', and filenames are appended unless 'pass_filenames: false' is set.\\n      \\n      Fully Supported Languages: Bun, Docker, Docker_image, Dotnet, Fail, Golang, Haskell, Julia, Lua, Node, Python, Ruby, Rust, Swift, Pygrep, System, Script, Deno\\n      (System is explicitly listed as fully supported)\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: /home/user/claude_skills/.pre-commit-config.yaml (lines 25-51)\\n  - Finding: File already contains multiple `language: system` hooks (conventional-pre-commit, repair-symlinks, check-symlinks, auto-sync-manifests, check-agent-auto-discovery, skilllint, check-compat-annotations, ty, enable-rerere) that are currently working in the repository\\n\\nEXPLANATION: Prek documentation confirms that `language: system` is fully supported. The current pre-commit config file demonstrates live usage of system language hooks working correctly with prek.\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: https://prek.j178.dev/languages/ (accessed 2026-04-25)\\n  CROSS_CHECK: .pre-commit-config.yaml (lines 25-51, current functioning hooks)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: WebFetch on 2026-04-25 + Read on 2026-04-25\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Goal**: Add a pre-commit hook that validates GitHub Actions workflow YAML structurally (beyond mere parsability), catching errors before push to GitHub.\\n**Assessed**: 2026-04-25T09:30:00Z (reassessment after fact-check and impact-analyst)\\n\\n**Conditions**:\\n\\n| # | Condition | State | Evidence or derivation path |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | .pre-commit-config.yaml exists and has check-yaml (parsability only), no structural validator | AVAILABLE | .pre-commit-config.yaml lines 61-62; fact-checker VERIFIED (claim 1) |\\n| 2 | 7 workflow files exist in .github/workflows/ (auto-rebase.yml, backlog-sync.yml, claude-code-review.yml, claude.yml, code-quality.yml, copilot-setup-steps.yml, quality-gate-audit.yml) | AVAILABLE | Initial snapshot verified via `ls .github/workflows/` |\\n| 3 | .claude/rules/ci-workflows.md Phase 4 uses YAML-syntax-only check (\\\"python3 -m yaml <file>\\\") | AVAILABLE | .claude/rules/ci-workflows.md lines 45-54; fact-checker VERIFIED (claim 2) |\\n| 4 | prek supports language: system local hooks | AVAILABLE | .pre-commit-config.yaml lines 25-51 (multiple existing system hooks); fact-checker VERIFIED (claim 6) |\\n| 5 | wrkflw validate command supports pre-commit hook integration (binary on PATH) | AVAILABLE | research/developer-tools/wrkflw.md lines 68-76; fact-checker VERIFIED (claim 3: JSON Schema validation, exit codes 0/1/2) |\\n| 6 | actionlint has a native pre-commit hook available (rhysd/actionlint repo) | AVAILABLE | github.com/rhysd/actionlint/.pre-commit-hooks.yaml; fact-checker VERIFIED (claim 5: three hook variants, pattern ^\\\\\\\\.github/workflows/) |\\n| 7 | Tool choice impacts CI portability (wrkflw=Rust/cargo, actionlint=Go binary) | AVAILABLE | research/developer-tools/wrkflw.md lines 36-37; fact-checker VERIFIED (claim 4: wrkflw 0.8.0 via cargo/brew) |\\n| 8 | `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml::file-hygiene` job runs prek on workflow files | AVAILABLE | code-quality.yml lines 171-192; impact-analyst cited with line range |\\n| 9 | `file-hygiene` job has explicit `SKIP` env var (line 185) for hook ids to exclude | AVAILABLE | code-quality.yml line 185; impact-analyst cited |\\n| 10 | New hook id must be added to `SKIP` list OR binary must be installed in CI for hook to run in CI | AVAILABLE | derived from code-quality.yml structure + impact-analyst risk assessment: hook's `files:` regex matches exactly the files this job processes |\\n| 11 | `.github/workflows/copilot-setup-steps.yml` installs prek hooks (line 55) | AVAILABLE | copilot-setup-steps.yml line 55; impact-analyst cited |\\n| 12 | actionlint / wrkflw binary availability on Copilot runner must be verified or hook must skip in CI | DERIVABLE | GitHub Actions Copilot environment documentation or test: add `- run: which actionlint` to copilot-setup-steps.yml and observe pass/fail. Alternatively: check official GitHub Copilot runner image spec at https://github.com/actions/runner-images/blob/main/images/ubuntu/... |\\n| 13 | `.github/actions/setup-python/action.yml` does not pre-install actionlint / wrkflw | AVAILABLE | setup-python/action.yml verified to install only uv + Python 3.11; impact-analyst verified |\\n| 14 | Binary dependency must be resolved before CI execution (either skip in `SKIP` list or pre-install) | AVAILABLE | derived from conditions 8-11 and impact-analyst risk chain |\\n| 15 | `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` Phase 4 instruction (line 51) must be updated or becomes stale | AVAILABLE | Fact-checker VERIFIED (claim 2: current instruction is YAML-syntax-only); impact-analyst identified staleness risk; agents will bypass structural validation if not updated |\\n| 16 | No automated test currently validates hook presence, `files:` scoping, or exit-code behavior | AVAILABLE | Impact-analyst verified test gap; measurable signal in item (inject `needs: [does-not-exist]` error) is manual-only; no CI job validates hook behavior |\\n\\n**Counts**: AVAILABLE 15, DERIVABLE 1, MISSING 0\\n**Verdict**: READY\\n\\n**Changes from snapshot**:\\n- Condition 5 (wrkflw validate support): DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE \u2014 fact-checker VERIFIED (claim 3) that wrkflw validate performs JSON Schema validation with exit codes 0/1/2\\n- Condition 6 (actionlint pre-commit hook): DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE \u2014 fact-checker VERIFIED (claim 5) that rhysd/actionlint/.pre-commit-hooks.yaml exists with three hook variants\\n- Condition 7 (tool choice portability): DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE \u2014 fact-checker VERIFIED (claim 4) that wrkflw 0.8.0 is installable via cargo/brew\\n- Conditions 8-16 (new scope from impact-analyst): ADDED \u2014 impact-analyst discovered file-hygiene CI job, copilot-setup-steps hook installation, and stale documentation risk that were not named in the initial snapshot. These conditions are all AVAILABLE or DERIVABLE (condition 12 only).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Alignment assessment: ALIGNED**\\n\\n### Mission Alignment\\n\\nThe proposed change adds a GitHub Actions structural validation hook to the pre-commit framework. This directly aligns with the Claude Code Marketplace Plugin mission of providing modular, language-agnostic development tooling. The feature improves the quality gate pattern already established in `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` by enabling **local** structural validation before git push, replacing the current require-push-and-observe feedback loop.\\n\\n**Evidence**: \\n- The repository's design principle (CLAUDE.md) states \\\"Engineering stance: Every edit improves product design. Errors and linting issues are architectural signals.\\\" Adding structural validation to pre-commit is exactly this kind of improvement.\\n- The feature directly supports the CI/CD quality gate pattern already documented in `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md`, which the harness mission depends on for reliable workflow execution.\\n\\n### Design Principle Alignment\\n\\nThe proposed change respects existing design patterns:\\n\\n1. **Pre-commit as the single validation source of truth** (`.pre-commit-config.yaml`, line 18-20): The feature adds a hook to the same framework used for all other quality gates (ruff, biome, markdownlint, ty, skilllint, etc.). This is consistent with the established pattern \u2014 all project linting runs through prek, not ad-hoc scripts. \u2713\\n\\n2. **Phase-gated CI protocol** (`.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md`): The CI workflow modification protocol already defines five phases, with Phase 4 stating \\\"Validate YAML syntax.\\\" The feature improves Phase 4 by replacing parsability-only validation with structural schema validation. This is an enhancement to the protocol, not a departure from it. \u2713\\n\\n3. **Prek language compatibility** (`.pre-commit-config.yaml`, lines 25-51): The hook will use `language: system` (already established pattern; 9 existing hooks use it). The new hook does not introduce a new language type or break prek compatibility. \u2713\\n\\n4. **File scoping pattern** (`.pre-commit-config.yaml`, line 105): The feature uses the same `files:` regex scoping pattern as markdownlint (`^(plan/|\\\\.claude/backlog/|\\\\.claude/BACKLOG\\\\.md)` vs the new `^\\\\\\\\.github/workflows/.*\\\\\\\\.ya?ml$`). This is consistent precedent. \u2713\\n\\n### Historical Alignment\\n\\n**Pattern precedent**: Examining the `.pre-commit-config.yaml` history and structure:\\n\\n- `skilllint` hook (line 144-151) \u2014 added to validate plugin/skill structure, runs on `plugins/` and `.claude/` files. This is a schema validator for a domain-specific format.\\n- `auto-sync-manifests` hook (line 127-133) \u2014 added to keep manifest files synchronized. This is a domain-specific quality gate.\\n- `check-agent-auto-discovery` hook (line 135-142) \u2014 guards against plugin.json misconfiguration. Another domain-specific structural validator.\\n\\nThe proposed actionlint/wrkflw hook follows the same pattern: **a domain-specific structural validator added to pre-commit when the repository maintains files of that domain** (GitHub Actions workflows in `.github/workflows/`). This is consistent with historical direction. \u2713\\n\\n**Documentation update precedent**: The `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` Phase 4 update (replacing \\\"YAML syntax only\\\" with \\\"structural validation\\\") mirrors the documentation-update pattern established when the CI Workflow Modification Protocol itself was created. Updates to Phase descriptions are the correct mechanism. \u2713\\n\\n### CI Integration Concerns\\n\\nThe item description and impact analysis identify a HIGH-risk interaction:\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml::file-hygiene` job has an explicit `SKIP` list (line 185) that must be updated to prevent the new hook from executing on CI runners where the binary (`actionlint` / `wrkflw`) is not pre-installed.\\n- The `copilot-setup-steps.yml` hook installation job may surface warnings or failures if the binary is not available.\\n\\n**Alignment perspective**: These are not alignment concerns \u2014 they are **scope/completeness concerns**. The proposed change is mission-aligned; the execution completeness (binary availability on CI runners, SKIP list updates) is an **operational concern**, not a design concern.\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\n**0 concerns identified \u2014 proposed change is consistent with product mission and historical direction.**\\n\\nThe feature:\\n- Enhances the existing CI quality gate pattern (consistent with mission)\\n- Follows established design principles for pre-commit hook organization and scoping (consistent with design)\\n- Matches the historical pattern of adding domain-specific structural validators when the repo maintains files of that domain (consistent with direction)\\n- Improves the Phase 4 validation instruction by replacing \\\"YAML syntax only\\\" with \\\"structural schema validation\\\" (consistent with protocol design)\\n\\n**Note on scope**: The item's Impact Radius section correctly identifies that `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml::file-hygiene` job and CI binary availability are **critical operational concerns** that must be addressed before merge (HIGH risk). These are not alignment divergences \u2014 they are implementation details that require careful execution in the CI Configuration phase. The design and intent are aligned; the grooming analysis has already surfaced the scope completeness gaps correctly.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add local github actions schema validation to pre-commit (actionlint or wrkflw)** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/wrkflw.md \u2014 pattern: Workflow Validation with Exit Codes (README line 101) and Integration Points (lines 591\u2013593)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:5cff073e6441ab85d7036d033cadbf2b -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-25)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nN/A for feature items \u2014 there is no broken behavior to reproduce. The gap is observable as an absence:\\n\\n1. Run `grep -E 'actionlint|wrkflw' /home/user/claude_skills/.pre-commit-config.yaml` \u2014 the command returns no output, confirming no structural validator is configured.\\n2. Create a test workflow file with a deliberate structural error (e.g., add `needs: [does-not-exist]` to any job in `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml`).\\n3. Run `uv run prek run --files .github/workflows/code-quality.yml` \u2014 prek exits 0 and no hook flags the invalid `needs:` reference.\\n4. Restore the test file.\\n\\nThe absence of a failing hook on step 3 is the observable gap this feature is designed to close.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Urgency is high because the gap is in the pre-commit quality gate that all developers and agents rely on. Every workflow change committed without structural validation is a push-and-hope cycle: errors surface only after git push triggers GitHub Actions. The CI Workflow Modification Protocol (`.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` Phase 4) is the agent-facing rule loaded during every workflow modification task; until this feature ships and Phase 4 is updated, agents are instructed to validate only YAML parsability \u2014 the exact failure mode this feature eliminates.\\n\\nEfect: P1 \u2014 primary quality gate gap with direct agent-instruction staleness risk.\\n\\nEffort: Small \u2014 additive hook entry to `.pre-commit-config.yaml` + one-line update to `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` Phase 4 + a CI SKIP-list decision. The feature does not change any existing hook, test, or code path.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Every developer and agent modifying `.github/workflows/*.yml` files \u2014 they receive no structural feedback before push.\\n- Bottleneck: The push-and-observe loop in `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` Phase 5 is the only current feedback path for workflow structure errors. Local validation is absent.\\n- Agent instruction risk: Agents loading `ci-workflows.md` Phase 4 during workflow modification tasks follow parsability-only validation guidance. After this feature ships but before Phase 4 is updated, agents will skip structural validation even though the hook exists.\\n- CI risk: The `file-hygiene` job in `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` (lines 171\u2013192) runs prek on workflow files. Its `SKIP` env var (line 185) must be updated or the binary installed in CI \u2014 omission creates a new CI failure category on every PR.\\n- Copilot runner risk: `.github/workflows/copilot-setup-steps.yml` installs prek hooks (line 55). If the structural validator binary is not on the Copilot runner PATH, hook installation surfaces warnings or failures.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Structural workflow errors (invalid `needs:` references, missing required keys, broken `${{ }}` expressions, malformed `uses:` syntax) are caught locally before commit \u2014 eliminating the push-and-observe feedback loop.\\n- `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` Phase 4 gate becomes accurate: agents follow structural validation guidance, not parsability-only.\\n- Consistent with the established pattern: `skilllint` validates plugin/skill structure, `check-agent-auto-discovery` validates plugin.json \u2014 this adds the equivalent domain-specific validator for GitHub Actions workflows.\\n- Developers with binary installed locally get sub-second structural feedback on every pre-commit run, not minutes waiting for a GitHub-side execution.\\n- Unblocks #1934 (trigger-aware diff filtering to local workflow validation), which requires this hook to be present as its target.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen the feature is present:\\n\\n- Running `uv run prek run --files .github/workflows/code-quality.yml` produces output that includes a row for the new structural validation hook, showing `Passed` status when the file is valid.\\n- Introducing a deliberate structural error to any workflow file (e.g., `needs: [does-not-exist]` referencing a non-existent job) and running `uv run prek run --files <that-file>` causes the hook to exit non-zero and report the offending job name and line number.\\n- Running `grep -E 'actionlint|wrkflw' .pre-commit-config.yaml` returns at least one match on a hook `id:` line.\\n- Valid workflow files (all 7 in `.github/workflows/`) pass the hook with exit 0.\\n- The hook fires only on files matching `.github/workflows/*.ya?ml` \u2014 it does not trigger on other YAML files in the repository.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `grep -E 'actionlint|wrkflw' /home/user/claude_skills/.pre-commit-config.yaml` returns at least one match on a hook `id:` line.\\n2. `uv run prek run --files .github/workflows/code-quality.yml` exits 0 and output includes a row for the new structural validation hook with status `Passed`.\\n3. Inject `needs: [does-not-exist]` as a job dependency in any workflow file, run `uv run prek run --files <that-file>` \u2014 hook exits non-zero and output names the offending job and line number. Restore the file after testing.\\n4. Running `uv run prek run --files README.md` does not trigger the new hook (the `files:` regex scopes it to `.github/workflows/*.ya?ml` only).\\n5. `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` Phase 4 no longer reads `python3 -m yaml <file>` as the sole validation step \u2014 it references the structural validation hook command.\\n6. The `file-hygiene` job in `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` either has the new hook id in its `SKIP` env var (line 185) OR the binary is verifiably available on the CI runner \u2014 the job does not fail on a clean PR touching workflow files.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|---|---|\\n| Skill | /python-engineering:pre-commit (hook schema reference for `.pre-commit-config.yaml` entries) |\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/research/developer-tools/wrkflw.md` \u2014 wrkflw validate exit codes, JSON Schema validation, integration patterns (lines 68-76, 375-393) |\\n| External | https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/.pre-commit-hooks.yaml \u2014 three pre-commit hook variants (Golang, Docker, system), all scoped to `^\\\\.github/workflows/` (verified 2026-04-25) |\\n| External | https://prek.j178.dev/languages/ \u2014 confirms `language: system` is fully supported (verified 2026-04-25) |\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/.pre-commit-config.yaml` lines 25-51 \u2014 nine existing `language: system` hooks as pattern precedent |\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` lines 171-192 \u2014 `file-hygiene` job with `SKIP` env var at line 185 |\\n\\n### Files\\n\\nFiles that must change for this feature to be complete (from Systems Inventory, HIGH-risk items starred):\\n\\n| File | Change type | Risk | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `.pre-commit-config.yaml` | CODE_CHANGE | LOW | New hook entry scoped to `^\\\\.github/workflows/.*\\\\.ya?ml$` |\\n| `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` | CONTENT_UPDATE | HIGH | Phase 4 line 51 must replace parsability-only check with structural validation command |\\n| `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` | CONFIG_UPDATE | HIGH | `file-hygiene` job `SKIP` env var (line 185) must include new hook id OR binary must be installed in CI |\\n| `.github/workflows/copilot-setup-steps.yml` | VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | MEDIUM | Binary availability on Copilot runner must be confirmed; hook installation (line 55) must succeed |\\n| `.github/actions/setup-python/action.yml` | VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | MEDIUM | Does not install actionlint/wrkflw; any CI job executing the hook needs the binary available |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 RT-ICA verdict READY; 15 AVAILABLE, 1 DERIVABLE (binary availability on Copilot runner \u2014 verifiable via runner image spec or a probe step), 0 MISSING.\\n- Blocks: #1934 (Add trigger-aware diff filtering to local workflow validation) \u2014 that feature requires the structural validation hook from this item to be present as its target.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 2/10 complexity.\\n\\nRationale:\\n- Primary change is an additive hook entry in `.pre-commit-config.yaml` \u2014 no existing hooks modified.\\n- Secondary change is a one-to-two line update in `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` Phase 4.\\n- Tertiary change is a CI `SKIP` list update in `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` (one line, one value).\\n- The only DERIVABLE condition (binary availability on Copilot runner) requires observation or a runner image lookup \u2014 not a code change.\\n- No new tests, no new services, no new dependencies beyond the binary itself.\\n- Highest effort component is the CI binary availability decision (SKIP vs install) \u2014 an intentional human or agent choice, not a complex implementation.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` \u2014 Phase 4 instruction is an agent-facing rule. When agents follow this file during workflow modification tasks (the exact use case of the CI Workflow Modification Protocol), they currently read \\\"Validate YAML syntax: `python3 -m yaml <file>` or equivalent\\\" and stop at parsability validation. After this feature ships but before the file is updated, any agent following Phase 4 will skip structural validation even though the hook now exists and would catch schema errors locally. This is the primary agent-instruction risk. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Phase 4 is a mandatory gate in the protocol (\\\"**Gate**: Changes committed and pass local validation\\\"). An incorrect gate instruction causes agents to commit workflow changes without structural validation, defeating the entire purpose of the feature.\\n\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/skills/pre-commit/SKILL.md` \u2014 This skill documents the pre-commit / prek framework and is consulted when modifying `.pre-commit-config.yaml`. It does not reference the specific hook inventory of this repository, so it does not become stale. However, if an agent uses this skill to implement the new hook and the chosen tool (`actionlint` or `wrkflw`) requires special configuration (e.g., `language: golang` for actionlint or `language: system` + cargo installation for wrkflw), the skill provides the hook schema reference needed. No update required to the skill itself. | Risk: LOW | Why: Skill documents generic framework, not repository-specific hook inventory.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml::file-hygiene` job (lines 171\u2013192) \u2014 The `file-hygiene` job runs `uv run prek run` against changed workflow files on every PR. Its `SKIP` env var (line 185) currently lists every hook name to exclude from the hygiene job. When the new `actionlint` hook is added to `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, the `file-hygiene` job will execute it on every push/PR unless the hook id is added to the `SKIP` list. Whether that is desired or not is a deliberate choice with CI consequences. | Risk: HIGH | Why: If the new hook id is not in `SKIP`, CI will attempt to run `actionlint` / `wrkflw` on the GitHub Actions runner. That binary must be pre-installed or available on `ubuntu-latest` for the step to succeed. Omission causes a new CI failure category. If added to `SKIP`, the hook only runs locally and the CI surface is unchanged.\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/copilot-setup-steps.yml` \u2014 Installs prek hooks (`uv run -q prek install`, line 55). If the new hook uses `language: system` with a binary like `actionlint` that is not on PATH in the Copilot environment, hook installation may fail or produce warnings. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: The copilot setup step validates the hook environment. A hook with an unresolvable `entry:` binary will surface as an installation warning or failure in this job.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `.github/actions/setup-python/action.yml` \u2014 Composite action that sets up `uv` + Python 3.11. Consumed by `code-quality.yml` jobs that run prek hooks. Does not install `actionlint` or `wrkflw`. If any CI job attempts to execute the new hook, the binary will be missing unless the setup action or job adds it. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: New hook creates a binary dependency not covered by the current setup composite. Any CI job that does not skip the new hook will fail with a `command not found` error.\\n\\n- `research/developer-tools/wrkflw.md` \u2014 The source research document cited in the item's Context section. The item references \\\"Workflow Validation with Exit Codes (README line 101) and Integration Points (lines 591\u2013593).\\\" This document is informational only and does not change; however, it is the evidence backing the `wrkflw validate` option. If `actionlint` is chosen instead, this file remains valid but its relevance to the implementation becomes indirect. | Risk: LOW | Why: Informational reference, not a runtime consumer.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml` \u2014 The file being directly modified to add the new `actionlint` / `wrkflw validate` hook entry. Currently hosts `check-yaml --unsafe` (lines 61\u201362) as the only workflow-file check. Adding the new hook changes the hook execution graph: every `prek run` invocation that touches `.github/workflows/*.yml` files now runs the new structural validator. Existing hooks are unaffected. | Risk: LOW | Why: Additive change only; existing hook entries are not modified. The new hook is scoped by the `files:` regex to `.github/workflows/*.ya?ml` so it cannot trigger on unrelated file types.\\n\\n- `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` \u2014 Phase 4 (line 51) instruction currently reads `\\\"Validate YAML syntax: python3 -m yaml <file> or equivalent\\\"`. This is the second directly-modified file. The update replaces parsability-only guidance with structural validation guidance (`uv run prek run --hook actionlint --files .github/workflows/<file>`). | Risk: LOW | Why: The file is a rules document consumed only as agent context. Change is a textual update to one instruction line; no code path depends on this file at runtime.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml::file-hygiene` job \u2014 This job runs prek with an explicit `SKIP` list (line 185). The current skip list names every hook id that should not run in the hygiene job. The new hook id (`actionlint` or `wrkflw-validate` \u2014 whatever id is chosen) must be evaluated for inclusion: either add to `SKIP` (hook runs locally only) or omit from `SKIP` and install the binary in CI (hook runs in CI too). This is an explicit CI configuration decision, not an automatic consequence. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Failure to decide and act creates a broken CI step. The `file-hygiene` job scope is exactly `.github/workflows/` files \u2014 the new hook's `files:` regex will match every file that job processes.\\n\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml::sync-pre-commit-deps` hook (line 19\u201322) \u2014 The `mxr/sync-pre-commit-deps` hook auto-updates `rev:` pins for remote repos when their dependencies change. If the new hook comes from a remote repo (e.g., `rhysd/actionlint`), `sync-pre-commit-deps` will manage the `rev:` pin automatically. If the hook uses `language: system` with a PATH binary (no `repo:` entry), `sync-pre-commit-deps` has no effect and the binary version is unmanaged. | Risk: LOW | Why: Configuration consequence to document in the hook entry, not a breakage risk.\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/copilot-setup-steps.yml` \u2014 Installs prek and validates toolchain. If the new hook binary is not available on the Copilot runner image, the setup step succeeds but subsequent hook execution fails. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Binary availability on the Copilot runner is not verified by any current step.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n\\n\\n### Documentation\\n\\n- `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` \u2014 Phase 4, line 51: `\\\"Validate YAML syntax: python3 -m yaml <file> or equivalent\\\"` will become factually inaccurate if left unchanged after the hook is added. Agents reading this rule file during workflow modification tasks will follow the old parsability-only instruction instead of running the new structural validator. Phase 5 line 64 (`\\\"Push and check workflow run if possible\\\"`) also becomes partially stale because the item's goal is to eliminate the push-required feedback loop with a local pre-commit alternative. | Risk: HIGH | Why: This file is loaded as a project instruction by agents modifying workflows. Stale guidance directly causes agents to miss the local validation step and fall back to push-and-observe, which is the exact failure mode this feature is designed to prevent.\\n\\n- `.claude/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 The project-level instructions reference `ci-workflows.md` explicitly: \\\"GitHub Actions CI Workflow Modification Protocol: `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md`\\\" (in the rules reference block). The CLAUDE.md text does not duplicate the Phase 4 content, so it does not need updating \u2014 it simply points to the rule file. But it confirms that `ci-workflows.md` is the authoritative agent instruction for all workflow modification work. | Risk: LOW | Why: The pointer remains accurate regardless of what is inside `ci-workflows.md`.\\n\\n- `research/developer-tools/wrkflw.md` \u2014 Section \\\"Relevance to Claude Code Development\\\" (lines 375\u2013393) describes use cases including \\\"Workflow validation in CI/CD pipelines\\\" and \\\"GitHub Actions skill validation.\\\" If `actionlint` is chosen over `wrkflw`, the research document does not need updating (it is a tool research entry, not implementation documentation). If `wrkflw` is chosen and the hook is added, the research document's claim about portability and Cargo dependency remains relevant to any CI integration decision. | Risk: LOW | Why: Research document; self-contained and correctly scoped.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible \u2014 `.pre-commit-config.yaml` requires the new hook entry\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible \u2014 `code-quality.yml` `file-hygiene` job `SKIP` list must be updated, or the binary must be installed in CI\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added \u2014 no automated test covers hook presence or exit-code behavior; manual validation is the only verification path (accepted gap or new test needed)\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated \u2014 `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` Phase 4 must be updated to replace parsability-only check with structural validation command\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated \u2014 `code-quality.yml` `SKIP` list and potentially `copilot-setup-steps.yml` binary installation\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated \u2014 `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` Phase 4 is the only agent instruction requiring update\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved \u2014 not a replacement scenario; additive hook\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked \u2014 binary availability on CI runners and Copilot environment verified before merge\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n\\n**Rationale**: The system currently allows GitHub Actions workflows with structural errors (malformed `needs:` references, missing required keys, unbalanced expressions, invalid `uses:` syntax) to pass pre-commit validation because only YAML parsability is checked. No schema validator exists in the pre-commit hook chain. This is not a broken implementation \u2014 it is the absence of a validation gate (actionlint or wrkflw) that should have been present from the start.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: N/A\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Malformed workflow files (missing `jobs:`, invalid `needs:` references, broken expressions) pass pre-commit and only fail at push time on GitHub \u2192 Malformed workflow files are caught locally before commit by actionlint/wrkflw schema validation in pre-commit\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n\\n- **Overall system risk**: MEDIUM\\n- **Highest-risk systems**:\\n  - `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` \u2014 `file-hygiene` job will attempt to run the new hook on CI runners where the binary (`actionlint` / `wrkflw`) is not installed, causing a new CI failure unless the hook id is added to `SKIP`\\n  - `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` \u2014 Phase 4 agent instruction becomes actively misleading after the hook ships; agents will skip structural validation and fall back to push-and-observe, defeating the feature's purpose\\n- **Main risk themes**:\\n  - operational: CI binary availability gap \u2014 `actionlint` / `wrkflw` is not in `ubuntu-latest` by default and not installed by `.github/actions/setup-python`\\n  - agent-instruction: Phase 4 instruction staleness causes agents to miss the local validation step this feature adds\\n  - verification: no automated test validates hook presence, correct `files:` scoping, or exit-code behavior on deliberate errors\\n- **Scope expansion**: The `file-hygiene` CI job was not named in the item description but is a direct consumer of the new hook. The `copilot-setup-steps.yml` hook installation job is a secondary consumer. Both must be addressed before the feature is complete.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n| Path | Role | Connection | Action | Risk |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `.pre-commit-config.yaml` | producer | Directly modified \u2014 new hook entry added | CODE_CHANGE | LOW |\\n| `.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` | agent-instruction / documentation | Phase 4 instruction becomes stale without update | CONTENT_UPDATE | HIGH |\\n| `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` | ci | `file-hygiene` job runs prek on workflow files; new hook id must be added to `SKIP` or binary must be installed in CI | CONFIG_UPDATE | HIGH |\\n| `.github/workflows/copilot-setup-steps.yml` | ci | Installs prek hooks; binary availability on Copilot runner unverified | VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | MEDIUM |\\n| `.github/actions/setup-python/action.yml` | configuration | Does not install `actionlint` / `wrkflw`; any CI job that executes the new hook needs the binary | VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | MEDIUM |\\n| `research/developer-tools/wrkflw.md` | documentation | Source evidence for the feature; no update needed but confirms tool choice implications | VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | LOW |\\n| `plugins/python-engineering/skills/pre-commit/SKILL.md` | agent-instruction | Documents hook schema; consulted when implementing new hooks; no stale claim | VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | LOW |\\n| `.github/workflows/auto-rebase.yml` | ci | No workflow file validation, unaffected | VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | LOW |\\n| `.github/workflows/backlog-sync.yml` | ci | No workflow file validation, unaffected | VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | LOW |\\n| `.github/workflows/claude.yml` | ci | No workflow file validation, unaffected | VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | LOW |\\n| `.github/workflows/claude-code-review.yml` | ci | No workflow file validation, unaffected | VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | LOW |\\n| `.github/workflows/quality-gate-audit.yml` | ci | No workflow file validation, unaffected | VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | LOW |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- None identified \u2014 there are no existing tests that validate the content or hook inventory of `.pre-commit-config.yaml`. The `validate-plugins` CI job (code-quality.yml lines 131\u2013143) runs `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/ .claude/` but does not validate hook presence or hook binary availability.\\n\\n  **Verification gap**: No test confirms that the new hook (a) exists in the config, (b) fires on `.github/workflows/*.yml` files, (c) exits non-zero on a deliberate structural error (the measurable signal described in the item). The acceptance criteria include injecting a deliberate `needs: [does-not-exist]` error and observing exit 1 \u2014 this is a manual validation step with no automated equivalent. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Without an automated test, hook regression (accidental removal, misconfigured `files:` pattern, wrong `entry:` command) would go undetected.\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\n`./.pre-commit-config.yaml` runs no GitHub Actions schema validator. The closest checks are `check-yaml` (lines 61-62) which validates raw YAML parsability only, and a generic `markdownlint-cli2` for docs. There is no hook that parses `.github/workflows/*.yml` against the Actions schema (jobs, steps, expressions, `uses:` references, `needs:` DAG validity).\\n\\n`./.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` Phase 4 (line 51) states \\\"Validate YAML syntax: `python3 -m yaml <file>` or equivalent\\\" \u2014 this is parsability only, not structural validation. Phase 5 (Verify) instructs \\\"Push and check workflow run if possible\\\" \u2014 i.e., the verification loop requires git push and observing GitHub-side execution. There is no local equivalent.\\n\\nSearch confirmed no existing backlog item references actionlint, wrkflw, or local Actions validation (`backlog_list search=\\\"github actions OR actionlint OR wrkflw\\\"` returned 0 items).\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\n`./.pre-commit-config.yaml` runs no GitHub Actions schema validator. The closest checks are `check-yaml` (lines 61-62) which validates raw YAML parsability only, and a generic `markdownlint-cli2` for docs. There is no hook that parses `.github/workflows/*.yml` against the Actions schema (jobs, steps, expressions, `uses:` references, `needs:` DAG validity).\\n\\n`./.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` Phase 4 (line 51) states \\\"Validate YAML syntax: `python3 -m yaml <file>` or equivalent\\\" \u2014 this is parsability only, not structural validation. Phase 5 (Verify) instructs \\\"Push and check workflow run if possible\\\" \u2014 i.e., the verification loop requires git push and observing GitHub-side execution. There is no local equivalent.\\n\\nSearch confirmed no existing backlog item references actionlint, wrkflw, or local Actions validation (`backlog_list search=\\\"github actions OR actionlint OR wrkflw\\\"` returned 0 items).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new `actionlint` (or `wrkflw validate`) hook is added to `./.pre-commit-config.yaml`, scoped to `^\\\\.github/workflows/.*\\\\.ya?ml$`. The hook fails with non-zero exit code when:\\n\\n- Required keys (`name`, `on`, `jobs`) are missing\\n- A `needs:` reference points at an undeclared job id\\n- `uses:` references an action with malformed syntax\\n- `if:` expressions contain unbalanced `${{ }}` or unknown context refs\\n- Composite-action inputs are missing required keys\\n\\n`./.claude/rules/ci-workflows.md` Phase 4 is updated: \\\"Validate workflow structure: `uv run prek run --hook actionlint --files .github/workflows/<file>`\\\" replaces the YAML-syntax-only check.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun: `uv run prek run --files .github/workflows/code-quality.yml`. Output includes a row for the new validation hook with status `Passed` or `Failed`. Inject a deliberate error (e.g., `needs: [does-not-exist]`) \u2014 hook reports exit 1 and names the offending job and line number. Without the error, hook exits 0.\\n\\n`grep -E \\\"actionlint|wrkflw\\\" .pre-commit-config.yaml` returns at least one match on a hook `id:` line.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nResearch entry: `./research/developer-tools/wrkflw.md`, \\\"Workflow Validation with Exit Codes\\\" section and \\\"Integration Points: GitHub Actions validation in CI/CD pipelines\\\".\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"6e09894e620b469ae2b088dcb2dd1c0eb1fdcb1e40516c19f54320cbc9a03547\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCUfJA\"}"}